 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "Rules are recorded as deferred callbacks on the bundle, then replayed against the app at registration.\n\n1. **Recording:** `Bundle.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`) is what the route decorators end up calling. It doesn't touch the app. It calls `Bundle.record(...)` (`bundles.py:224`) with a lambda, which appends to `self.deferred_functions`.\n2. **Registration entry:** `App.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `bundle.register(self, options)`.\n3. **Replay:** `Bundle.register` (`bundles.py:273`) does the following:\n   - Checks the name against `app.bundles` and stores the bundle there.\n   - Builds a `BundleSetupState` via `make_setup_state` (`bundles.py:246`).\n   - Runs each deferred function with that state (`bundles.py:334-335`).\n   - Registers nested bundles recursively, passing down combined `url_prefix`, `subdomain` and `name_prefix`.\n4. **Applying to the app:** each deferred lambda calls `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`bundles.py:87`). It does the following:\n   - Prepends `url_prefix` to the rule.\n   - Defaults the subdomain.\n   - Merges `url_defaults`.\n   - Prefixes the endpoint as `{name_prefix}.{name}.{endpoint}`.\n   - Calls `App.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:606`), which adds the rule to `url_map` and stores the view in `view_functions`.\n\nThe static route for bundles with a static folder goes through the same `state.attach_route_rule` path (`bundles.py:323-328`).",
